# Use Cases

Each use case sized to its scenario. **Per-use-case question count matters; total is whatever it ends up being** (~200 across all UCs at current sizing). Sorted by Normain mode.

**Uniqueness** = how much of this test exercises capabilities that aren't already covered by another use case. Higher = more distinctive contribution. Subjective.

| # | Use case | Mode | Persona | Scenario | Question types | # docs | # questions | Uniqueness | What it tests |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | Due diligence financial review | Simple | PE / corp dev analyst reviewing a target | Verify financials, spot red flags, cross-check numbers between annual report, proxy, and Excel model | Numerical calc; cross-doc (10-K vs proxy); Excel step-by-step logic; reasoning on covenants/warning signs | 6 | 15 | **30%** — Excel logic unique; numerical + cross-doc overlap with several others | Numeric extraction + cross-doc consistency + chained reasoning |
| 06 | Multimodal evidence extraction | Simple | Advisory / forensic analyst | Single mixed-format corpus; varied Qs pull facts from scans, photos, charts, handwriting | OCR-grade text from scans; handwriting recognition; image-only chart interpretation; cross-modal reconciliation | 4 | 10 | **90%** — only test covering scanned, handwritten, image-only formats | Format coverage — exposes tools that can't ingest non-text inputs |
| 07 | M&A data-room deep dive | Simple | M&A counsel / investment committee chair | 10 deep synthesis questions over a target's full data room (red flags, hidden liabilities, change-of-control exposure, IP issues, regulatory risk, key-employee dependencies, customer concentration, litigation, off-balance-sheet items, MAC triggers) | Synthesis across many docs; risk identification; pattern detection; gap identification at scale | **100+** | 10 | **85%** — depth × scale combo; tests context-window survival + lost-in-the-middle | Reasoning across very large corpora — Normain's strongest competitive wedge |
| 02 | ESG / sustainability audit | Repeat | Sustainability lead prepping CSRD, or auditor | Same Qs across multiple companies' sustainability reports → comparison table | Exhaustive search; numerical aggregation; multi-doc cross-reference (report vs framework) | 4 | 15 | **35%** — framework-vs-disclosure alignment angle | Long-doc exhaustive extraction + framework alignment |
| 04 | Contract clause sweep at scale | Repeat | Legal ops / M&A counsel | Same clause-finding Qs across **100+ contracts** in a bundle → per-contract comparison table. Real-customer scale | Exhaustive (find every X); classification; clause-level citation fidelity; cross-contract pattern detection | **100+** | 20 | **70%** — only Repeat-at-scale test; exposes per-doc-count limits in competitors | Repeat-mode scale ceiling + clause-level citation across hundreds of docs |
| 03 | Regulatory-vs-policy gap check | Spreadsheet | GRC / internal audit | Each row = one obligation from the regulation; columns assess policy coverage with citations | Cross-doc (reg vs policy); exhaustive requirements enumeration; classification; reasoning on partial coverage | 6 | 15 | **55%** — per-obligation structured enumeration | Cross-doc reasoning + exhaustiveness + citation fidelity |
| 05 | Vendor / supplier risk matrix | Spreadsheet | GRC / vendor management / TPRM lead | Each row = one vendor; columns score risk dimensions using vendor's SOC2 + public disclosures + ToS | Cross-doc per vendor; classification (risk tier); per-column varied questions; citation across short security docs | ~15 | 15 | **65%** — vendor TPRM scenario unique | Per-row varied prompting + cross-doc per entity + risk classification |
| 08 | DDQ / questionnaire response | Spreadsheet | Sales engineer, compliance lead, IR ops responding to a customer/investor questionnaire | A buyer/auditor sends a 100-question DDQ (operational due diligence, SIG, CAIQ, RFP). Each row = one question; answer + citation + confidence pulled from the org's own documentation pack (policies, SOC2, ISO, prior questionnaires, product docs) | Structured answer generation; citation from own corpus; classification (in-scope / out-of-scope / partial); consistency across related questions | ~25 | **100** | **75%** — only test with very high question count on one corpus; structured-questionnaire workflow is a flagship Normain scenario | Question-volume ceiling + structured response from a single-org corpus |

**Total**: 8 use cases, ~200 questions, ~270+ docs.

## Mode coverage

- **Simple** (3): UC01, UC06, UC07
- **Repeat** (2): UC02, UC04
- **Spreadsheet** (3): UC03, UC05, UC08

All three Normain modes covered.

## Scale stress points

| Stress | Use case | Why it matters |
|---|---|---|
| **High question volume on one corpus** | UC08 (100 Qs on ~25 docs) | DDQ/questionnaire workflow — real Normain use case |
| **Many docs, repeat mode** | UC04 (100+ contracts, 20 Qs) | Per-doc context isolation at scale |
| **Few questions, deep synthesis on huge corpus** | UC07 (10 deep Qs spanning 100+ docs) | Lost-in-the-middle, citation drift, context overflow |
| **Multimodal** | UC06 | Format ingestion ceiling |
| **Spreadsheet-mode per-row varied prompting** | UC03, UC05, UC08 | Three different shapes of structured row-by-row work |

## Grading workload note

~200 questions × ~10 competitors = ~2000 grading events. Roughly double the original 100-Q estimate. LLM-judge first-pass remains feasible; human stratified sample grows from ~30 to ~50 questions × all competitors to keep statistical power.
